 text.push_str("\nAt32workers, A uses8.73%fewer cycles and8.06%fewer instructions in the separate counter panel; B2 cycles increase0.80%and instructions fall0.14%. B2 branch misses increase17.03%, while generic cache misses fall2.49%. None identifies a cache level, DRAM bandwidth or an exclusive critical-path fraction. The low retained payload does not guarantee lower latency.\n\n| Profile | Samples | Unknown share | Lost |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
 for q in["A","B"]{for w in[16,32]{for label in["control","candidate"]{let p=&a["profiles"][format!("cycles-1x2-{q}-w{w}-{label}")];writeln!(text,"|{q}/{w}/{label}|{}|{:.3}%|0|",p["samples"],p["unknown_share"].as_f64().unwrap()*100.).unwrap();}}}
 text.push_str("\nAll18,307samples have the fixed16Mperiod, expected executablePID, registered worker/caller TID, workerFORK/task evidence, matching binaryMMAP and permitted CPU. All recordings have zero lost records. Candidate A-w16 has978samples and is retained as small-sample context. Profiles remain dominated by the same stream/apply, reduction and inverse kernels; G2 coalesce_run is visible. Symbol shares include inlined work and are not removable walltime. Absolute sampling coverage is not validated.\n\n## Validation and retained failures\n\nThe177-file private snapshot has170byte-identical original files, six append-only parents with exact prefix recovery, and one private child. All176production files and field arithmetic remain unchanged. Three newly executed focused native tests pass (125unaffected core tests filtered): original-classifier equivalence, mapped-span point ownership, complete weighted-generator results, optional-allocation denial/fallback, identity/cancellation/doubling exceptions, ragged tile/partition boundaries, and repeated1/4/16/32worker queries on512KiB stacks. Existing field/core qualification is inherited, not rerun or claimed as a new complete suite. No portable/prover/huge/concurrent-proof qualification is inferred.\n\nAll four real populations bind to independent complete Arkworks MSM oracles. Two new A references were needed because the older A ordinary-window bucket checks omit top and final weighting. B2 full references are reused byte-for-byte. No new witness solve, proof or Gnark export occurs. All400caller processes check3primes, every timed result and1post:12,024complete weighted-query outputs. Inputs stay unchanged, routes/counts/payloads stay stable, and worker affinity is checked. Source, library, driver, oracle, fixture and protocol pins match.\n\nAn initial pre-capture symbol audit expected an out-of-line prepare symbol, which had been inlined; it stopped before any caller ran. Only the audit expectation changed to the linked classifier symbol; runtime routes provide activation evidence. Initial helper/log retained. Native5-step, consumer4-step and capture440-step workflows each finish once. Eight planned chown commands affect only generated perf.data ownership before32read-only decoders. No capture/test/oracle is repeated.\n\nThe first offline reviewer incorrectly assumed link-sdk plan entries contain argv, as command entries do. Its failed source/log remain; the corrected reviewer checks generated rustc arguments, library/driver identities and flags separately. This bookkeeping repair changes no capture or candidate. Successful review independently checks449raw command/exit/stream receipts,1,505pin entries, original source recovery, all route/payload/output receipts, paired wall/CPU/RSS statistics, all counter values, every sample and symbol bin, exact executablePID/TID/CPU/MMAP/FORK evidence and the failed gate. It reruns no query, oracle or proof.\n\n## Accepted proof comparisons — inherited, unchanged\n\n");
 let old=fs::read_to_string("/home/ubuntu/src/zk-tools/zopro/docs/benchmarks/2026-10-30-bounded-coalesce176/README.md").unwrap();let start=old.find("|Shape|Accepted ms|").unwrap();let end=start+old[start..].find("\n[Design]").unwrap();text.push_str(&old[start..end]);
 text.push_str("\n\nAll eight CPU10×targets remain unmet. No SDK/full-proof trial follows this failed query gate. This exact sparse overlay is closed for high-core adoption; its solo/16worker A gains are retained as evidence, not selected as an adopted subset. A future change needs a distinct measured operation or dependency reduction, not an unchanged rerun. No new AWS resources, Aeglos comparison, minimumRAM, phone/ARM/TEE, swap, huge-circuit or throughput result follows.\n\n[Design](artifacts/design.md), [prospective capture protocol](artifacts/capture-design.md), [all observations](artifacts/analysis.json), [symbol profiles](artifacts/symbols.json), [independent review](artifacts/review.json), [source audit](artifacts/source-audit.json), [binary identities](artifacts/identities.json), [linked-code check](artifacts/codegen.json), [fixture/oracle provenance](artifacts/fixtures.json). Archives: [private source](artifacts/source.tar.gz), [helper/protocol sources](artifacts/workflow.tar.gz), [all raw command receipts and counter CSVs](artifacts/receipts.tar.gz), [disassembly](artifacts/codegen.tar.gz). [Checksums](SHA256SUMS).\n\nPrivate point/scalar/key arrays, executables, libraries and perf.data stay local with retained hashes. No witness-derived output point is published. [Accepted implementation and qualification](../2026-10-30-g2-vector-sign-adoption176/README.md).\n");
